		(property "Description" "Three sprung battery contacts: one negative dome on the well floor and TWO positive tabs on the wall. Both positives must see 3 V to boot; only the left carries the logic current, the right is sensed at ~50 nA. This is the connector-less battery interface and there is no catalogue land pattern for it.  [pinout: bom/bom.json BATT-CONTACTS; docs/REFERENCE-TEARDOWN.md 2.5 (O'Flynn: the big pads under the terminals are NOT connected; the real contacts are the small pads under the tabs).]"
